Z||000006||StuGood||09-30-2000||03:18 PM||||If it makes you feel better,you're not alone, frontal.  My clock seems to change times, too.  Approximately once a minute    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sorry... couldn't resist.  Seriously, does your clock keep resetting to 1:00 every time you switch on the ignition?  If so, and if it forgets the station presets, it could mean the radio "keep alive" quit.  Sometimes a connector or fuse.  It's same fuse as horn, dome light and cigarette lighter. <P>I hope you can fix yours, doc, because I've been anxiously awaiting your cue, for me to hook up my battery    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ! <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-02-2000).]||||reg||5
